//
// SMC Verilator coverage scope. Passed to Verilator at compile time from
// [coverage.verilator].build_args in smc_sim_cfg.toml, so what it drops never
// enters the coverage database. Edit then `--rebuild`.
//
// Scope is applied at COMPILE time: a report-time filter prunes the pages and
// still grades the whole database.
//
// This file grades what SMC owns: hw/sys/smc/rtl, hw/sys/smc/regs, the hw/top
// shells and the cov/sv points. The VCS scope in ../vcs/smc_cov_scope.hier is
// wider -- it follows the SEP rule and keeps functional third-party IP graded
// -- so the two flows report different populations; ../vcs/README.md says why
// the public-CI set stays narrow.
//
// MECHANISM NOTE: Verilator's `coverage_off` takes `-file` (with globs) only.
// There is no `-module` form -- `coverage_off -module "prim_rom"` is a syntax
// error.
//
// GLOB NOTE: the pattern is matched against the path as Verilator OPENED the
// file, not the absolute path it records in the generated code. The filelist
// is absolute but files reached through `+incdir+` are opened relative, so a
// pattern must cover both forms. `*vendor/*` matches either; `*/vendor/*`
// matches only the absolute form and silently leaves the rest instrumented.
// Never put a `/` straight after the leading `*`.
//
// DO NOT add hw/sys/smc/dv/cov/sv/* here. Those files carry the
// OCAH_FCOV_COVER points that populate the `user` metric family; excluding
// them would delete the functional coverage this flow exists to collect.

`verilator_config

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Testbench code. Not the DUT, must not be scored.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// tb_top.sv is the TB body itself (SEP drops the same thing with
// `-tree sep_uvm_top 1`). The cov/sv modules it instantiates are separate
// files and stay instrumented.
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/smc/dv/tb/tb_top.sv"
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/smc/dv/tb/smc_tb_if.sv"
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/smc/dv/tb/verilator_stubs/*"
// DV collateral bound into smc_ip_integration: counters, FW mailbox, ECC
// inject hook, image backdoors.
coverage_off -file "*hw/sys/smc/dv/models/*"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Chipyard-generated CPU cluster.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Generated third-party RTL that only the CPU-reaching tests exercise; the
// same argument SEP used to drop `sep_uvm_top.u_dut.u_sep.u_sep_cpu`.
// VCS equivalent: -tree smc_uvm_top.u_dut.u_smc.u_smc_cpu_wrapper.u_smc_cpu
coverage_off -file "*chipyard_generated_files/*"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Vendored third-party RTL.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// pulp-platform axi + common_cells, chipsalliance i3c-core, lowRISC prims,
// tt-hw-debug trace/mmr. The public-CI figure is SMC-owned RTL; the VCS scope
// keeps the functional blocks among these graded.
coverage_off -file "*vendor/*"

// IP blocks and shared primitives SMC integrates carry their own DV packages
// and their own coverage; SMC grades the integration it owns (rtl/, regs/ and
// the cov/sv points), the same rule the SMU and DTP scopes apply.
coverage_off -file "*hw/ip/*"
coverage_off -file "*hw/common/*"

// KNOWN GAP: this line drops chipsalliance/i3c-core and lowRISC/opentitan,
// but not vendor/pulp-platform/** or vendor/tenstorrent/tt-hw-debug/**, which
// stay instrumented. No file pattern reaches them; `*pulp-platform/*` and
// `*tt-hw-debug/*` are inert here. The scoped denominator is therefore larger
// than a complete vendor exclusion would give. ../vcs/README.md carries the
// measurement method.
